  "caption": "Quinn's ankle has had its own weather forecast ever since an old sprain: creaky first steps, grumpy stairs, no deep squats.\n\nAnkle arthritis often follows an old injury, and it's managed much like knee arthritis. Walking doesn't wear it out faster.\n\nWhat can help: strengthening the calf, hip and knee, keeping fit with cycling, swimming or water walking, firm, slightly rockered soles so the foot rolls through, and gentle daily movement to keep the range you have. On flare days, walking poles and a lighter plan can help before building back up.\n\nIf the ankle becomes hot, red and swollen without an injury, see your GP promptly.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
